    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy today hinges on capitalizing on soft matchups against high-xERA starters. **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) stands as our premier play; he benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and faces Tanner Bibee, whose delivery rhythm provides a distinct advantage for **Gunnar Henderson** regarding stolen base upside\u2014a critical factor for our scarcity-weighted scoring. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.27) follow closely as elite options. **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-ceiling outing against the struggling Riley Cornelio (5.59 xERA), while **Kyle Tucker** remains an anchor despite a neutral platoon matchup against Nick Lodolo, as his elite base projection holds firm regardless of handedness.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was the exclusion of **Wade Meckler** (47.03), who narrowly missed the cut behind the dynamic speed threat of **Nasim Nunez** (48.87). While **Wade Meckler** offered a decent park factor, his L/L platoon disadvantage against Patrick Sandoval ultimately penalized his efficiency score, pushing him to the bench in favor of the versatility provided by **Nasim Nunez**. We are also keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Drake Baldwin** (60.91); while both are currently slated for high-value spots, their exact batting order remains pending. If **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin** drop significantly in the lineup after official postings, we may see their scores fluctuate, though their respective matchups against AJ Smith-Shawver and Freddy Peralta provide enough cushion to keep them active. We remain thin on impact depth due to ongoing IL designations for **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**, forcing us to lean heavily on the consistency of the active core to maintain our Roto standing.",
